/-! # Proper closed carriers and scheme-theoretic support

Source: Stacks Project, Spaces Perfect, Tag 0CZI, (2) iff (3); Morphisms of Spaces,
Tags 07U0 and 07U1; Tag 03MB for the structure-quotient case
(blueprint: lem-sfb-space-module-proper-carrier-support).

The annihilator is characterized on every object and every further restriction of the
small etale site. Its ideal equals the kernel of the support's structure quotient map.
Thus the support is specified with its full closed-subspace structure.
-/

@[expose] public noncomputable section

set_option autoImplicit false

universe u

open CategoryTheory CategoryTheory.Limits Opposite

namespace AlgebraicGeometry.AlgebraicSpace

/-- The annihilator of a finite type quasi-coherent module is quasi-coherent, cuts out
its scheme-theoretic support, and that support is proper exactly when the module has a
finite type quasi-coherent realization on a proper closed carrier.
Source: Stacks Project, Tags 07U0, 07U1 and 0CZI(2) iff (3)
(blueprint: lem-sfb-space-module-proper-carrier-support).

Proof:
1. On etale scheme charts use lem-trf-scheme-zariski-etale-quasi-coherent-equivalence
and lem-sfb-space-qcoh-affine-chart-calculus. The scheme annihilator is quasi-coherent
by lem-weil-pbc-scheme-theoretic-support. Chart changes are flat by
def-weil-etale-morphism, so lem-trf-annihilator-finite-flat-base-change identifies the
restricted annihilator ideals. Their inclusions are equal, so the cocycles hold.
Apply lem-sfb-space-qcoh-cartesian-chart-family to descend the ideal A. Its sections
are exactly the functions killing every section after every further restriction.
2. By lem-sfb-space-ideal-closed-subspace-correspondence, A cuts out C. The module is
annihilated by A; lem-sfb-space-closed-immersion-quasi-coherent-modules descends it to
C. For any other closed carrier W its ideal annihilates M and is contained in A.
The inclusion-reversing ideal correspondence gives a closed inclusion C into W.
3. The descended module on C is finite type: restrict to etale scheme charts using
lem-trf-space-etale-module-pushforward-restriction, compare etale and Zariski modules,
and apply lem-weil-pbc-closed-immersion-pushforward-annihilated. Fully faithfulness
identifies the descended module with that tensor pullback. Finite type descends from
these charts by lem-sfb-space-qcoh-affine-chart-calculus. If C is proper this gives the
required carrier.
4. Conversely C is closed in every carrier W by step 2. Closed immersions are proper
by lem-sfb-space-closed-subspace-proper; compose with W to Y using
lem-sfb-space-proper-composition, forgetting S to the absolute base if needed.
This uses neither a Noetherian nor a flatness assumption. -/
theorem module_proper_carrier_support {S : Scheme.{u}} {X Y : AlgebraicSpace S}
    (f : X ⟶ Y) (hf : MapIsLocally (@LocallyOfFiniteType) f)
    (M : X.Modules) (hMq : M.IsQuasicoherent) (hMt : M.IsFiniteType) :
    ∃ (A : QuasiCoherentIdeal X) (C : ClosedSubspace X),
      (∀ (U : X.EtaleSite) (a : X.structureSheaf.obj.obj (op U)),
        a ∈ Set.range (A.val.arrow.val.app (op U)) ↔
          ∀ (V : X.EtaleSite) (r : V ⟶ U) (s : M.val.obj (op V)),
            X.structureSheaf.obj.map r.op a • s = 0) ∧
      A.val = kernelSubobject (moduleStructureMap C.val.arrow) ∧
      (MapIsProper (C.val.arrow ≫ f) ↔
        ∃ (W : AlgebraicSpace S) (j : W ⟶ X) (G : W.Modules),
          IsRepresentableWith (fun _ _ p ↦ IsClosedImmersion p.left) j.hom.hom ∧
          MapIsProper (j ≫ f) ∧ G.IsQuasicoherent ∧ G.IsFiniteType ∧
          Nonempty ((moduleDirectImage j).obj G ≅ M)) := by
  sorry

/-- For any closed subspace, its direct-image structure module is finite type and
quasi-coherent, its annihilator cuts out precisely that subspace, and it admits a proper
closed carrier exactly when the subspace is proper over the target.
Source: Stacks Project, Tag 03MB, Tags 07U0 and 07U1, and Tag 0CZI(2) iff (3)
(blueprint: lem-sfb-space-module-proper-carrier-support).

Proof:
5. By lem-sfb-space-closed-ideal-correspondence the structural direct image is O_X/I,
where I is the kernel ideal. It is quasi-coherent; on affine etale charts it is R/I,
generated by 1, so lem-sfb-space-qcoh-affine-chart-calculus makes it finite type.
A local function annihilates this quotient exactly when it kills 1, equivalently when
it belongs to I, and the same holds after every restriction. The closed-ideal bijection
therefore identifies its scheme-theoretic support with the original closed subspace.
Apply module_proper_carrier_support to this module for the proper-carrier equivalence.
In particular this argument allows non-finitely-generated ideals and nilpotents. -/
theorem structure_module_proper_carrier_support {S : Scheme.{u}}
    {X Y : AlgebraicSpace S} (f : X ⟶ Y)
    (hf : MapIsLocally (@LocallyOfFiniteType) f) (C : ClosedSubspace X) :
    ((moduleDirectImage C.val.arrow).obj
      (SheafOfModules.unit (C.val : AlgebraicSpace S).structureSheaf)).IsQuasicoherent ∧
    ((moduleDirectImage C.val.arrow).obj
      (SheafOfModules.unit (C.val : AlgebraicSpace S).structureSheaf)).IsFiniteType ∧
    (∃ A : QuasiCoherentIdeal X,
      A.val = kernelSubobject (moduleStructureMap C.val.arrow) ∧
      ∀ (U : X.EtaleSite) (a : X.structureSheaf.obj.obj (op U)),
        a ∈ Set.range (A.val.arrow.val.app (op U)) ↔
          ∀ (V : X.EtaleSite) (r : V ⟶ U)
            (s : ((moduleDirectImage C.val.arrow).obj
              (SheafOfModules.unit (C.val : AlgebraicSpace S).structureSheaf)).val.obj (op V)),
            X.structureSheaf.obj.map r.op a • s = 0) ∧
    ((∃ (W : AlgebraicSpace S) (j : W ⟶ X) (G : W.Modules),
      IsRepresentableWith (fun _ _ p ↦ IsClosedImmersion p.left) j.hom.hom ∧
      MapIsProper (j ≫ f) ∧ G.IsQuasicoherent ∧ G.IsFiniteType ∧
      Nonempty ((moduleDirectImage j).obj G ≅
        (moduleDirectImage C.val.arrow).obj
          (SheafOfModules.unit (C.val : AlgebraicSpace S).structureSheaf))) ↔
      MapIsProper (C.val.arrow ≫ f)) := by
  sorry

end AlgebraicGeometry.AlgebraicSpace
